#+TITLE: CAD instance probes reuse A/B drawings across Windows runs
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+BRANCH: codex/cad-probe-unique-20261023

* Reproduction and cause
The Windows probe scripts/probe-cad-instances.ps1 saves both logical
instances to TEMP/cadinst-<backend>-A.dwg and -B.dwg. A second probe under
the same account reuses those names. If an earlier CAD still holds a
file, SaveAs encounters a lock; cleanup also names the shared files.
Observed on pfenny on 2026-10-23; its BricsCAD Recent Paths includes
cadinst-bricscad-B.dwg and Windows Recent contains cadinst-autocad-A/B.
The producer was identified in CI checkout 52f52cb9, on
cad-launch-new-by-default; it was absent from the older working clone.

* Resolution
Allocate a private directory and filenames containing the backend,
PowerShell PID, a fresh GUID and A/B. SaveAs, ROT lookups and cleanup all
use the same path map. Never pre-delete a shared legacy filename.
Cleanup removes only that probe's exact DWG/DWL/DWL2 paths and removes the
directory only when empty, preserving unexpected files.
The macOS probe already allocates its private directory with mktemp.

* Validation
scripts/tests/test-probe-cad-instances-paths.ps1 extracts and executes the
real helpers without launching CAD. Two allocations in the same process
produce four distinct filenames; cleanup of one preserves the other one's
drawings and locks, a legacy A drawing, and an unexpected file. Both
AutoCAD and BricsCAD variants pass under PowerShell 7 on macOS and
Windows PowerShell on pfenny. Both Windows native probe jobs run this
check before launching CAD. The full native probe was not rerun by this
correction, avoiding interference with existing CAD activity.
